Subject: [PATCH] cap_gemini_live: vendor the Gemini Live voice component

The Gemini Live voice capability (toggle-on/off conversation via the
BidiGenerateContent WebSocket) is a JarvisNano-authored component that
does NOT exist upstream in espressif/esp-claw. Because esp-claw/ is a
gitignored, pinned clone, any source created directly inside it is lost
on a clean re-clone (and `clone_or_update_esp_claw` will refuse to move
off the pinned ref while uncommitted local files are present).

This patch makes the component reproducible. The canonical source is
git-tracked at:

    firmware/components/cap_gemini_live/
      CMakeLists.txt
      idf_component.yml
      include/cap_gemini_live.h
      include/cmd_cap_gemini_live.h
      src/cap_gemini_live.c
      src/cmd_cap_gemini_live.c

scripts/bootstrap.sh copies it into the generated tree at
  esp-claw/components/claw_capabilities/cap_gemini_live/
via the new copy_cap_gemini_live() step (same idiom as copy_board /
copy_firmware_assets), registered in main() before the apply_* chain.

The component is wired into the build behind CONFIG_APP_CLAW_CAP_GEMINI_LIVE:
  - apply_gemini_live_main_require_patch() adds `cap_gemini_live` to
    main/CMakeLists.txt main_requires.
  - main.c includes cap_gemini_live.h and runs touch_monitor_task, which
    calls cap_gemini_live_toggle() on each finger-down (tap-to-talk).

Protocol audit notes captured in this revision (verified 2026-05-21 against
ai.google.dev, docs updated 2026-05-13):
  - Model id: models/gemini-3.1-flash-live-preview (was the superseded
    2.5-era models/gemini-2.5-flash-native-audio-preview-12-2025).
  - Thinking config: generationConfig.thinkingConfig.thinkingLevel:"minimal"
    (3.1 replaced the 2.5-era thinkingBudget integer; setting both is a 400).
  - realtimeInput.audio.{mimeType,data} is the current send field (NOT the
    older mediaChunks); serverContent.modelTurn.parts[].inlineData carries
    24 kHz PCM16 audio out; turnComplete / interrupted drive state.

NOTE: this is a documentation record of a generated-tree mutation, not a
unified diff against tracked files. The mechanism is the cp in
scripts/bootstrap.sh:copy_cap_gemini_live(), mirroring patches/0009's
documentation-of-a-bootstrap-mutation convention.
